---
/*
  Privacy policy.

  Written to describe what this site actually does rather than to recite a
  template. Every processor named below is one the site genuinely uses — an
  inaccurate privacy policy is worse than none, because it is a published
  statement a regulator can hold you to.

  Kept indexable. A privacy page is a trust signal that search quality raters
  and buyers both look for, and hiding it defeats the point of having one.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const description = `How ${site.name} handles personal data: what the contact form collects, which processors are used, how long data is kept, and how to have it deleted.`;

// Stated so the page carries its own currency rather than implying it is
// maintained more often than it is.
const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description={description} ogRoute="default">
  <section class="wrap pt-10 pb-12 md:pt-14">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[]} current="Privacy" />

    <p class="eyebrow mt-8">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-[2.4rem] leading-[1.05] md:text-[3.4rem]">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-lg text-[var(--color-ink-2)]">
      What we collect, why, and how to get rid of it. Last updated {lastUpdated}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap pb-16">
    <div class="post-body max-w-2xl">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is a workflow automation agency operating under {site.parent}.
        For anything in this policy, contact
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="link-underline">{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Contact form submissions.</strong> If you use the contact form we
        receive your name, email address, company name, an approximate team size,
        and whatever you write in the message field. You choose all of it. We ask
        for nothing else and there are no hidden fields beyond a spam honeypot,
        which is never read as personal data.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Vercel Analytics and Vercel Speed
        Insights. Both are cookieless and do not fingerprint visitors or build
        cross-site profiles. They report aggregate page views and performance
        timings. We cannot identify you from them, and neither can we tie a page
        view to a contact form submission.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host records standard request logs,
        including IP addresses, as part of operating the site. The contact
        endpoint also holds an IP address in memory briefly to rate-limit
        submissions. It is not written to a database and does not survive a
        restart.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We set no advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
        <li>We do not sell, rent or share your data with advertisers.</li>
        <li>We do not run remarketing or ad-network pixels.</li>
        <li>We do not add you to a mailing list because you filled in the form.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
      <p>
        We keep the list short deliberately — every processor is somewhere your
        data could go, so we use as few as the site needs.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — hosting, serverless functions, analytics.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivers contact form submissions to our inbox.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Workspace</strong> — where that email is then received and stored.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers operate internationally, so your data may be processed
        outside your own country, including in the United States.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we are allowed to hold it</h2>
      <p>
        Contact form data is processed on the basis of legitimate interest:
        you asked us about work, and answering requires holding what you sent
        long enough to reply. Analytics is aggregate and cookieless, so it does
        not rely on consent under GDPR or ePrivacy.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries stay in our email for as long as the conversation is live and
        for up to 24 months afterwards, so we can pick up a thread you left open.
        Ask us to delete it sooner and we will. Records tied to paid work are
        kept for as long as accounting rules require.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live you can ask for a copy of what we hold, ask
        us to correct it, ask us to delete it, or object to us holding it at all.
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="link-underline">{site.email}</a>
        and we will action it within 30 days. You do not need to explain why, and
        asking will not affect any live conversation.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are in the UK or EU and think we have handled this badly, you can
        complain to your national data protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2>Client systems we build</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers this website only. When we build automation for a
        client, that client remains the data controller for anything flowing
        through it; we act as a processor under the terms of that engagement,
        and credentials and infrastructure sit in the client's own accounts.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially we update the date at the top. We do
        not backdate it to look freshly maintained.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .post-body :global(h2) {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .post-body :global(p) {
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .post-body :global(ul) {
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    list-style: disc;
  }
  .post-body :global(li) {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
